.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-archive-set-create 1  "tapectl-archive-set-create " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-archive\-set\-create \- Create a new archive set policy
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl archive\-set create\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-copies\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-required\-locations\fR] [\fB\-\-encrypt\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-compression\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-checksum\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-slice\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-verify\-interval\-days\fR] [\fB\-\-warehouse\-copies\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new archive set policy
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-copies\fR \fI<MIN_COPIES>\fR
Minimum copy count
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-required\-locations\fR \fI<REQUIRED_LOCATIONS>\fR
Required locations (comma\-separated)
.TP
\fB\-\-encrypt\fR \fI<ENCRYPT>\fR
Encryption enabled
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-compression\fR \fI<COMPRESSION>\fR
Compression mode
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-checksum\-mode\fR \fI<CHECKSUM_MODE>\fR
Checksum mode
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-slice\-size\fR \fI<SLICE_SIZE>\fR
Slice size (e.g., "2400G")
.TP
\fB\-\-verify\-interval\-days\fR \fI<VERIFY_INTERVAL_DAYS>\fR
Verify interval in days
.TP
\fB\-\-warehouse\-copies\fR \fI<WAREHOUSE_COPIES>\fR
Warehouse copies expected (ADR\-0006). Omitted leaves the field NULL, which means "defer to the system default"
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Description
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Archive set name
